.TH WERKMEISTER-CACHE 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-cache \- Prune the shared build and package caches (\fBcaches:\fR in the registry) by each one's age or prune rule
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister cache\fR <action> [name]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-reset\fR
Empty the cache(s) instead of applying the rule.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Prune a cache even while a running container mounts it.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what would be deleted; change nothing.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Applies each shared cache's rule from the registry's \fBcaches:\fR: \fBmax_age\fR deletes older entries, \fBprune\fR runs the tool's own command. \fB\-\-reset\fR empties the cache instead. A cache that a running container mounts is skipped unless \fB\-\-force\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister cache prune
werkmeister cache prune \-\-dry\-run
werkmeister cache prune \-\-reset
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
